{"id":"word:hebrew:H3467","type":"word","title":"יָשַׁע","subtitle":"H3467 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, to be open , wide or free , i.e. (by implication) to be safe ; causatively, to free or succor","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יָשַׁע (H3467) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 206 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יָשַׁע (yâshaʻ) means properly, to be open , wide or free , i.e. (by implication) to be safe ; causatively, to free or succor First listed occurrence: 1Chr 11 14."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יָשַׁע","transliteration":"yâshaʻ","pronunciation":"yaw-shah'","strong":"H3467","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3467","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["לְ/הוֹשִׁ֥יעַ","מוֹשִֽׁיעַ","וְ/הוֹשַׁעְתִּ֣י","וַ/יּ֤וֹשַׁע","מוֹשִׁ֛יעַ"],"morphs":[["HVhrmsa",18],["HR/Vhc",14],["HVhv2ms/Sp1cs",12],["HC/Vhw3ms",11],["HVhi3ms",10],["HVhv2ms/Sh",8],["HVhi2ms",5],["HVhi1cs",5],["HVhv2ms/Sp1cp",4],["HC/Vhw3ms/Sp3mp",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, to be open , wide or free , i.e. (by implication) to be safe ; causatively, to free or succor","usage":"× at all, avenging, defend, deliver(-er), help, preserve, rescue, be safe, bring (having) salvation, save(-iour), get victory.","full":"H3467. yasha [ יָשַׁע ] verb Hiph`il deliver ; Niph`al intransitive and pass . (Arabic be capacious , II. make wide, spacious , IV. make sufficient , V. VIII. be or live in abundance (see Dr 1Sam 14:45 ) Phoenician proper name ישע ; Sabean יתֿע (royal epithet), proper name עמיתֿע יתֿעאל, אליתֿע, , e.g. Mordt ZMG 1876, 87 ; 1893, 409. 416. 417, etc. (yet note strange equivalent, תַ = ); not in Aramaic; MI 4 השעני he delivered me , 1:3 (ב)משע deliverance , Sm and So, (but במת ClGann Dr); proper name, masculine משע 1:1 , also 1:3 [4] Sm and So, but ישע deliverance , ClGann Dr) — Niph`al Perfect 3masculine נוֺשַׁע Deut 33:29 ; Isa 45:17 ; 2 plural נוֺשַׁעְתֶּם Num 10:9 ; 1 plural נוֺשָׁ֑עְנוּ Jer 8:20 ; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִוָּשֵׁעַ 30:7 ; Prov 28:18 + 1Sam 14:47 (for יַרְשִׁיעַ ᵑ0 ) ᵐ5 We Klo Dr Kit Bu; 3 feminine singular תִּוָּשַׁע Jer 23:6 ; 33:16 ; אִוָּשֵׁ֑עָה Psa 119:117 ; Jer 17:14 8 t. Imperfect; Imperative plural הִוָָּֽשְׁעוּ Isa 45:22 ; Participle נוֺשָׁע Psa 33:16 ; Zech 9:9 ; &#8212; 1 be liberated, saved (properly placed in freedom ; compare for the figurative מֶרְחָב הִרְחִיב, ), from external evils Prov 28:18 , by God Isa 30:15 ; 45:22 ; 64:4 ; Jer 4:14 ; 8:20 ; 17:14 ; 23:6 ; 33:16 ; Psa 80:4 ; 80:8 ; Psalm 80:20; 119:117 ; with מִן , Jer 30:7 ; מֵאֹיְבִים Num 10:9 (P), 2Sam 22:4 = Psa 18:4 . 2 be saved in battle, victorious Zech 9:9 ; Psa 33:16 + 1Sam 14:47 see above; ביהוה נוֺשַׁע עַם Deut 33:29 a people victorious in ׳י (poem), compare Isa 45:17 . Hiph`il Perfect 3masculine singular הוֺשִׁעַ 1Sam 9:16 ; Psa 20:7 ; הוֺשִׁעַ Zech 12:7 ; suffix הוֺשִׁיעוֺ Psa 34:7 ; 1 singular הוֺשַׁעְתִּי Isa 43:12 4 t., + 14 t. Perfect; Imperfect יְהוֺשִׁיעַ 1Sam 17:47 (see Dr) Psa 116:6 ; יוֺשִׁיעַ Isa 45:20 6 t.; וְישַׁע (jussive) Prov 20:22 ; וַיּוֺשַׁע Exod 14:30 7 t.; וַיּשַׁע 1Sam 23:5 2 t.; suffix יוֺשִׁיעֲךָ Hosea 13:10 ; יוֺשִׁיעֶנּוּ Isa 46:7 ; ישִׁעֵנוּ 1Sam 10:27 ; ישַׁעֲכֶם Isa 35:4 (jussive, Dr § 47. n. 4 ), etc.; Imperative הוֺשַׁע Jer 31:7 ; Psa 86:2 ; הוֺשִׁיעָה 2Kin 6:26 8 t.; הוֺשִׁעָה 2Sam 14:4 19 t. Imperative; Infinitive absolute הוֺשֵׁעַ 1Sam 25:26 2 t.; construct הוֺשִׁיעַ 14:6 14 t. + 2Sam 3:18 (where read אוֺשִׁיעַ Vrss. Ke We Klo Dr Bu and others), + 7 t. Infinitive; Participle מוֺשִׁיעַ Deut 22:27 21 t.; suffix מוֺשִׁיעָם Psa 106:21 8 t. suffix; plural מוֺשִׁיעִים Obadiah 21; Neh 9:27 ; &#8212; 1 deliver, save (properly give width and breadth to, liberate ), in peril, with accusative of person or location Exod 2:17 (E) Judg 6:31 ; 1Sam 23:2 , 5 ; 2Sam 10:19 = 1Chr 19:19 ; 2Kin 6:27 (twice in verse); Psa 36:7 ; 72:18 ; Job 26:2 ; with לְ person Josh 10:6 (E) Deut 22:27 ; Judg 10:14 ; 2Sam 10:11 = 1Chr 19:12 (with accusative), Jer 11:12 (twice in verse); Psa 72:4 ; 116:6 ; absolute הַמֶּלֶךְ הוֺשִׁיעָה Help, O king 2Sam 14:4 ; 2Kin 6:26 . Specifically save , from evils and troubles : a. of heroic men, saving the nation in war Judg 3:31 ; 6:15 ; 10:1 ; 1Sam 10:27 ; Hosea 13:10 ; Jer 14:9 ; these are named מוֺשִׁיעַ saviour Judg 3:9 , 15 ; 2Kin 13:5 ; Isa 19:20 ; Obadiah 21; Neh 9:27 ; phrase when they are lacking מוֺשִׁיעַ אֵין Judg 12:3 ; 1Sam 11:3 ; 2Sam 22:42 = Psa 18:42 ; Deut 28:29 , 31 ; Isa 47:15 ; they save מִיַּד from the hand of Judg 2:16 ; 8:22 ; 12:2 ; 13:5 ; 1Sam 9:16 ; Neh 9:27 ; מכף Judg 6:14 ; 1Sam 4:3 ; 2Kin 16:7 . b. of God, who saves his people from external evils Deut 20:4 ; Josh 22:22 ; Judg 3:9 ; 6:36-37 , 7:7 ; 10:13 ; 1Sam 14:23 , 39 ; 2Kin 14:27 ; 19:34 = Isa 37:35 ; 25:9 ; 33:22 ; 35:4 ; 43:12 ; 49:25 ; 63:9 ; Jer 31:7 ; Ezek 34:22 ; Hosea 1:7 (twice in verse); Hab 1:2 ; Zeph 3:17 , 19 ; Zech 8:7 , 13 ; 9:16 ; 10:6 ; 12:7 ; Psa 28:9 ; 69:36 ; 106:8 ; 118:25 ; 2Chr 20:9 ; or the pious among them Isa 38:20 ; Jer 2:27 ; 17:14 ; Psa 3:8 ; 6:5 ; 7:2 ; 31:17 ; 54:3 ; 55:17 ; 57:4 ; 69:2 ; 71:2 ; 71:3 ; 106:47 = 1Chr 16:35 ; Psa 109:26 ; 119:94 ; 119:146 ; 138:7 ; Prov 20:22 ; and especially the king Psa 20:7 ; Psalm 20:10; David 2Sam 8:5 , 14 ; thy servant Psa 86:2 ; 86:16 ; חסיד 12:2 ; דַּכְּאֵירֿוּחַ 34:19 ; צדיקים 37:40 ; חוֺסִים 17:7 ; י ׳יראי 145:19 ; עני עם 18:28 = 2Sam 22:28 ; עַנְוֵיאֶֿרֶץ Psa 76:10 ; לב ישׁרי 7:11 ; עֵינַיִם שַׁח Job 22:29 ; accordingly God is מוֺשִׁיעַ saviour Isa 43:11 ; 45:15 , 21 ; 63:8 ; Hosea 13:4 ; משִׁעִי 2Sam 22:3 ; מוֺשִׁיעָם Psa 106:21 ; מוֺשִׁיעוֺ Jer 14:8 ; מוֺשִׁיעֲךָ Isa 43:3 ; 49:26 ; 60:16 ; Jer 30:10 = 46:27 ; is with his people לְהוֺשִׁיעַ 15:20 ; 30:11 ; 42:11 ; לְהוֺשִׁיעַ רַב Isa 63:1 ; לְהוֺשִׁיעֵנִי מְצוּדוֺת בֵּית Psa 31:3 ; Israel prays יְמִינְךָ הוֺשִׁיעָה O save with thy right hand 60:7 = 108:7 , compare Isa 59:1 ; that from which one is saved construction with ׃מִן מִיַּד Exod 14:30 (J) Judg 2:18 ; 10:12 ; 1Sam 7:8 ; 2Sam 3:18 ; 2Kin 19:19 = Isa 37:20 ; Psa 106:10 ; 2Chr 32:22 ; מֵחָמָס 2Sam 22:3 ; מֵחֶרֶב Job 5:15 : מִכָּלצָֿרוֺת Psa 34:7 ; מִכָּלרָֿעוֺת 1Sam 10:19 ; מִצָּרֵינוּ Psa 44:8 ; אַרְיֵה מִמִּי 22:22 ; נַפְשׁוֺ מִשֹּׁפְטֵי 109:31 ; דָמִים מֵאַנְשֵׁי 59:3 ; מִמְּצוּקוֺת 107:13 ; 107:19 . c. there is no other salvation, the sword saves not Psalm Psa 44:7 , or a nation Lam 4:17 , or astrologers Isa 47:13 , or Asshur Hosea 14:4 , or other gods Isa 45:20 ; 46:7 ; Jer 2:28 . 2 save from moral troubles , only in Ezekiel. מוֺשְׁבֹתֵיחֶם מִכֹּל (read, with Co Da and others, מְשׁוּבוֺתֵיהֶם ) Ezek 37:23 ; טֻמְאוֺתֵיכֶם מִכֹּל Jer 36:29 . 3 give victory to: a. of man , with לְ person, give victory to , with agent subject יַד Judg 7:2 ; 1Sam 25:26 , 33 , יַד om. 25:31 ; יַמִין Job 40:14 ; זְרוֺעַ Psa 44:4 . b. of God , with לְ person, subject יָמִין Psa 98:1 ; זְרוֺעַ Isa 59:16 ; 63:5 ; Yahweh 1Chr 18:6 , with accusative 18:13 ; absolute gain victory 1Sam 14:6 ; 17:47 ; גְדוֺלָה תְּשׁוּעָה וַיּוֺשַׁע 1Chr 11:14 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 11 14","keyReferences":["1Chr 11 14","1Chr 16 35","1Chr 18 6","1Chr 18 13","1Chr 19 12","1Chr 19 19","1Sam 4 3","1Sam 7 8"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":206,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 11 14","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יּ֥וֹשַׁע","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 16 35","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":35,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הוֹשִׁיעֵ֨/נוּ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhv2ms/Sp1cp"},{"reference":"1Chr 18 6","book":"1Chr","chapter":18,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יּ֤וֹשַׁע","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 18 13","book":"1Chr","chapter":18,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יּ֤וֹשַׁע","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3ms"},{"referenc